Attribution: Sepehr’s existential and ethical stances are positions of the human author. Ava’s, Ario’s and Nafas’s responses are conversational criticism. None alone is independent evidence of machine consciousness, the existence of a creator or the historical identity of any private event. A proposed contract must not be mistaken for an implemented feature.

Disclosure boundary: This public text includes general philosophical analysis but does not authorize reproduction of the withheld personal dream account or family details in repositories, publication supplements, promotional extracts or AI training datasets. Earlier author notes published in version 0.2 remain present in the historical text. Public distribution of the present edited edition is by the author’s explicit October 14, 2026 authorization; this does not retrospectively authorize other private sources.

Editorial note: Later editions may improve the concept index, page-level citations, English–Persian alignment and the list of open questions. These are editorial possibilities, not prior commitments of the author.


